          "path": "_m/g/c/q/v/derby-cathedral-wp/view-derby-cathedral-e.jpg",
          "filename": "Derby Cathedral England.JPG",
          "caption": "View of Derby Cathedral, England, looking west from Cathedral Green. The 65m high tower dates from the 1530s, the nave from 1725 and the retrochoir from the 1970s. The latter is made from artificial sandstone, whereas the nave and tower are of Derbyshire Millstone Grit. A peregrine falcon nest platform is just visible in lower left corner of bell tower louvres. Cathedral Green was redeveloped and opened as a new public open space in 2009. A statue of Bonnie Prince Cahrlie on horseback is visible in the extreme left of the image",
          "alt": "View of Derby Cathedral, England, looking west from Cathedral Green. The 65m high tower dates from the 1530s, the nave from 1725 and the retrochoir from the 1970s. The latter is made from artificial sandstone, whereas the nave and tower are of Derbyshire Millstone Grit. A peregrine falcon nest platform is just visible in lower left corner of bell tower louvres. Cathedral Green was redeveloped and opened as a new public open space in 2009. A statue of Bonnie Prince Cahrlie on horseback is visible in the extreme left of the image",
